					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1056717#post-2175281</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1056717/sunset#post-2175281</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 09 Dec 2014 08:06:41 +0000</pubDate>
								<wikidot:authorUserId>1361261</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>The writing itself was fine, the descriptions of the monsters attacking Sol were pretty good, albeit without the sort of larger context one expects from an existential threat to <em>the Sun</em>. So I can see people being entertained by this.</p> <p>What it comes down to for me, really, is the fact that I can't take SCP-1548 seriously at all, especially when it's paired alongside SCP-179, a serious article that I like.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
